 health zone (Lwandiko, Mahembe, Kagulwe, Kabeya, Kahoho, Babinza, Matama, Bulungu, Mkungandala, Mukosamali)","evidence":"The forested Lulenge/Kimbi area straddling the Fizi-Kabambare border is a long-standing operating area of Mai-Mai groups (CNPSC/Yakutumba and allied factions, now largely aligned with Wazalendo) with limited state presence; the specific controlling faction per village is unknown.","unit":"CD6309-kabambare","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"contesting"},{"entity_id":"cnpsc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[153,159]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Kabambare secteur, centre and west (Kabambare centre/Mbundu, Sombe, Lubambi, Mwanamwamba, Katemema, Kazabu, Shabimba, Kiyanga)","evidence":"Kabambare centre is the territorial administrative seat with police and an FARDC presence; no reports of armed-group control of the town or its western hinterland were found in prior knowledge.","unit":"CD6309-kabambare","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[166]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Lusangi secteur (Lukoma/Lusangi, Muzingandu, Nyezi, Muyombo, Kasesa, Ayuza, Kavima) toward Kasongo and Kongolo","evidence":"No significant armed-group control reported for Lusangi secteur; state administration and police posts assumed in the main villages.","unit":"CD6309-kabambare","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[166]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Western Salamabila secteur around Wamaza (Mutakuya/Wamaza, Kiviluka, Kawaya, Mulozi, Kingombe, Mwangundu, Mayembe)","evidence":"Wamaza is a large gold-mining town with state administration, police and FARDC posts; Malaika activity is reported mainly further east around Salamabila/Namoya. Default state presence with possible Malaika incursions.","unit":"CD6309-kabambare","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"mm-malaika","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[166]},{"controller_id":"mm-malaika","sovereign_id":"mm-malaika","status":"contested","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","since":"2017","zone":"Rural central/eastern Salamabila secteur (Kayembe, Kihonya, Amusini, Salumu-Basikibunda, Agenda) and Tengetenge villages of Lusangi health zone","evidence":"Mai-Mai Malaika is based in the forested hinterland of Salamabila secteur, taxing artisanal gold sites and villages and periodically clashing with FARDC. Exact village-level control is not documented; assigned by proximity to Malaika's known area of operation. No source could be fetched for this run.","unit":"CD6309-kabambare","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"contesting"}],"source_ids":[159,166]},{"controller_id":"cod-fardc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"contested","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Salamabila town (Kitoko, Lubinga, Akilibangi, Kimputu, Kopakopa, Matchapano) and the Namoya gold-mine area (Matete), Saramabila health zone","evidence":"Salamabila centre and the Namoya mine concession have had a permanent FARDC deployment since Mai-Mai Malaika (Sheikh Hassan) began attacking the Banro-operated mine around 2017-2019; Malaika has repeatedly raided the town outskirts and mining camps. Assessment from background knowledge of UN GoE and Radio Okapi reporting; web research tools were unavailable, so no 2026 confirmation.","unit":"CD6309-kabambare","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-pnc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"mm-malaika","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[159,166]}],"sources":{"153":{"url":"https://www.kivusecurity.org/","title":"Kivu Security Tracker (incident map)","publisher":"Kivu Security Tracker"},"159":{"url":"https://www.un.org/securitycouncil/sanctions/1533/work-and-mandate/expert-reports","title":"UN Group of Experts on the DRC final reports (2019-2025): CNPSC/Yakutumba, Twirwaneho and Mai-Mai in Fizi, Itombwe and Minembwe","publisher":"United Nations Security Council","date":"2025-06-01"},"166":{"url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/tags/kabambare","title":"Radio Okapi – Kabambare tag (Mai-Mai Malaika incursions in Salamabila, FARDC operations, Kabambare centre)","publisher":"Radio Okapi","date":"2025-12-31"}},"units":{"CD6309-kabambare":"Kabambare territory (Maniema) is mostly state-administered in its western Lusangi secteur and around Kabambare centre and Wamaza, with police the main day-to-day authority. The Salamabila secteur in the north-east is the stronghold of Mai-Mai Malaika, which has fought the FARDC around Salamabila town and the Namoya gold mine since ~2017; the army holds the town and mine area while Malaika dominates parts of the forest hinterland. The far east toward Fizi (Lulenge/Kimbi) is a Mai-Mai/Wazalendo operating area with weak state presence. NOTE: web research was unavailable for this run (search budget exhausted, fetch domains blocked), so all zones rest on prior knowledge and are low confidence."}}